NEWS ANNOUNCER: ...repeating our critical warning. State meteorologists confirm that the Super Typhoon has maintained its catastrophic strength upon approach. A massive storm surge—estimated between five to seven meters high is expected to inundate coastal areas within the next few hours. Repeat - this is not ordinary flooding. If you are in low-lying coastal zones, evacuate immediately-

PILI: Why...
PILI: Why did you turn it off?! Ernesto, did you hear what he said? Five to seven meters! That is higher than our roof! 
PILI: Mercy wasn't just panicking! The city, the radio, the weather bureau..
PILI: All of them! They are all saying the same thing!

ERNESTO: Because it's poison, Pili! It's nothing but panic-mongering from people who have never stepped foot in Taklub! 
ERNESTO: They warned us about a 'tidal wave' last September and what happened? The water barely reached the bottom step of our porch! 
ERNESTO: They use these heavy English words just to make fools out of us!

ERNESTO: I am trying to keep us from starving! 
ERNESTO: If I abandon this harvest tonight, who is going to pay the forty thousand pesos we owe for the fertilizer? Who?! The Mayor? Mercy? The reporters in Manila? NO!

PILI: We can always rebuild, Ernesto! 
PILI: We can find a way! But we can't rebuild our children if they are dead!

ERNESTO: Rebuild with what?!
ERNESTO: This land, this house, these crops-
ENRNESTO: This is everything I have built with my bare, bloodied hands! 
ERNESTO: I am doing EVERYTHING that I can so that you all can have food in the table and live a good life!
ERNESTO: If we lose the contract, the traders will take this land. They will take this roof from over our heads.
ERNESTO: Where will we go then? On the highway? 
ERNESTO: I am the provider of this house and I am telling you, WE ARE NOT GOING ANYWHERE!
ERNESTO: WE STAY! 

PILI: ...
PILI: ...
PILI: You and your god damn pride....
PILI: You care more about your crops than the blood in your children's veins.

ERNESTO: ...
ERNESTO: Go check on the kids. We are staying.

PILI: If the water takes them tonight... 
PILI: I will never forgive you. 
PILI: May God have mercy on us.


