DODONG: Tita Mercy just likes using her megaphone because she's the barangay captain. 
DODONG: And please, Tatay said it’s gonna be fine. 
DODONG: Remember last summer when the water came up to the porch?
DODONG: We made paper boats and raced them down the lane. It was fun! Right, Noni?

NONI: Yeah! I want to make a big blue boat tomorrow for Kuya Ollie's birthday if it happens!

VALERIE: Hey... Listen to Ate... three of you. 
VALERIE: You don't need to worry about Tatay and Nanay shouting, okay? They’re just tired from all the birthday preparations. 
VALERIE: And you know how strong Tatay is, right? He built this entire house with his own hands. 
VALERIE: Your house is not going anywhere.
VALERIE: So we have to be very good, okay? We have to stay close together so Tatay and Nanay don't get stressed out.
VALERIE: We only have each other to rely on.
VALERIE: We have to stay together...
VALERIE: We have to...

NONI: So the rain won't break Kuya's birthday banners?

VALERIE: Not a chance. Ate tied them super tight earlier. 
VALERIE: Tomorrow, we are still going to have spaghetti, chocolate cake...all of those food.
VALERIE: We are still going to celebrate Ollie turning eight. 
VALERIE: But tonight, we just need to be the best team ever. Dodong, you're the second eldest, okay? I need you to help me watch over Kiki. 
VAELRIE: If the rain gets too loud and she starts crying, you give her her favorite toy. Can you do that for me?

DODONG: Yeah! I can do that, Ate. I'll take care of Kiki.

KIKI: Baaah!

DODONG: Are we really staying here, Ate?

VALERIE: If we all stay close and follow the rules, everything is going to be perfectly fine. 

VALERIE: Ate is right here, okay?
VALERIE: I'm not going anywhere.
